## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Can I see when my Android phone was last unlocked?
A: No. Android has no unlock history. Digital Wellbeing shows how many times the phone was unlocked today, but not when, and not by whom.

### Q: How do I know if someone opened my phone while I was asleep?
A: Check Digital Wellbeing in the morning. Screen time or app use during the night that isn't yours is the clearest sign. On Samsung you can see screen time per hour.

### Q: Can someone go through my phone without leaving a trace?
A: Mostly, yes, if they know what to clear: browser history, recent apps and Google activity can all be deleted. Digital Wellbeing's counts are harder to hide. A photo taken at the moment of a wrong PIN can't be undone by the person, because it's already in your inbox.

### Q: How do I catch someone snooping on my phone?
A: Change your PIN so they have to guess, and install an app that photographs wrong unlock attempts, like CrookCatcher. You get a photo, the time and the location by email.

### Q: Is there an app that shows who unlocked my phone?
A: Apps can't see who used a correct PIN or fingerprint, but they can react to failed attempts. CrookCatcher takes a photo after a wrong PIN, pattern or password, and Pro's break-in detection also covers a correct guess that follows a wrong one.

### Q: Does a factory reset remove someone's access to my phone?
A: Changing your PIN, removing unknown fingerprints and logging out linked devices is usually enough. Also change your Google password if you saw a device you don't recognize in your Google Account.

